cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the Zenodo DOI of the corresponding release (linked on the GitHub Releases page)."
title: "BioELM: A Backprop-Free Language Model with Local Learning Rules"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zeng
    given-names: Naiqi
    email: X005_0001_0001@163.com
repository-code: "https://github.com/X005-0001-0001/BioELM"
url: "https://github.com/X005-0001-0001/BioELM"
license: AGPL-3.0
abstract: >-
  BioELM is a language model trained entirely without autograd / backpropagation.
  Learning is driven by exact online RTRL eligibility traces on a diagonally-structured,
  selectively-gated SSM, combined with three-factor local updates and a meta-Adam rule.
  The system is released as self-contained single-file programs and evaluated against a
  conventional TinyGPT2 under identical wall-clock, data and hardware budgets.
keywords:
  - local learning
  - RTRL
  - no backpropagation
  - language model
  - biologically plausible
